// Generated from cmake/build_manifest.h.in -- do not edit.
//
// What went into this build: versions, the commit, the compiler, the licence terms. §58.7
// asks the Python wheel for it and §38 asks a baseline manifest for the exact runtime
// version of the encoder, and those are the same facts, so they are gathered once here
// rather than twice in two build files.
//
// Every value is read from the build. None of it can be recovered from a binary afterwards,
// and all of it is the first thing a bug report or a calibration run needs.
//
// On the version fields: libx264 and libx265 are linked statically, so what pkg-config
// reported at configure time is also what runs. For a backend whose encoder lives in a
// driver -- oneVPL, VA-API -- that is not true and there is no field for it here; see
// docs/STATUS.md on why the baseline calibration covers the software backends first.

